{title: Holy, Holy, Holy}
{artist: Reginald Heber}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
[G]Early in the [D]morning our [A]song shall rise to [D]thee.
Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Merciful and [D]mighty!
[G]God in three [D]persons, [A]blessed Trini[D]ty!

Verse 2
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! All [G]saints adore Thee,
[G]Casting down their [D]goldcrowns around the [A]glassy sea; Cherubim and [D]serphim
falling down [Bm]before [G]Thee, Who [D]was,
[G]and is, and [D]evermore [A]shall be.

Verse 3
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! though [G]darkness hide Thee,
[G]Though the eye of [D]sinman Thy [A]glory may not see; Only [D]Thou
art holy; [Bm]there is [G]none beside [D]Thee,
[G]Perfect in pow'r, in [D]love, [A]and purity.

Verse 4
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! Lord [G]God Almighty! All
[G]Thy works shall [D]praise Name, in [A]earth, and sky, and [D]sea;
Holy, holy, [Bm]holy; [G]merciful and [D]mighty!
[G]God in three [D]Persons, [A]blessed Trinity!
